CHANGES RELATIVE TO EMWM 2.1
----------------------------

Removed: the backdrop subsystem, which mapped a window over the root and hid
anything drawn there by feh(1), xsetroot(1) and similar; XSMP session
management and its client database; the _MWM_WM_REQUEST property protocol;
"standard behavior" mode and its four duplicate resource tables; the
cppCommand resource; and a large amount of code behind preprocessor macros
that no makefile defined.

Added: an internal session facility (f.logout, f.reboot, f.shutdown,
f.suspend) backed by user-configurable commands, with an optional idle lock
timer; f.rename_workspace, replacing the removed protocol's NAMWKSPC verb;
an extended rc file format with Settings, Client and Workspace blocks, so
behaviour is configured in one place and the X resource database carries
appearance only; EWMH dock, strut and sticky support; and optional
integration with stalonetray.

Unchanged on purpose: X atom names. _MOTIF_WM_HINTS, _MWM_WM_HINTS,
_MWM_WORKSPACE_*, WM_STATE, WM_PROTOCOLS and the _NET_* set are the
interoperability contract that Motif and other toolkits rely on. Renaming
them would break every client that speaks them.
